# ============================================================================
# TC-WEB-005  Unmatchable query resolves via autosuggest, never dead-ends
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Objective : A query with no literal match still lands the user on a populated,
#             usable results page rather than a blank or broken one.
# Platform  : web          Priority : P2
# Suite     : suites/web_regression_suite.json
# Params    : base_site, junk_search_term
#
# WHAT THIS DOES *NOT* TEST — read before editing:
#   This is not an empty-state test, and it cannot be made into one with
#   `search for`. The `search()` helper in execution/action_service.py types the
#   term, then looks for an <li> matching it and CLICKS that suggestion, only
#   falling back to Enter when none is visible. JustDial's AI autosuggest
#   answers even nonsense terms, so the suggestion path is always taken and the
#   `trkid=ai-auto` parameter appears in the resulting URL.
#
#   So the real behaviour under test is: autosuggest absorbs an unmatchable
#   query and still delivers a working results page. That is worth guarding —
#   a regression here means a blank page or a crash for fat-fingered searches.
#   Testing a genuine no-results state needs a submit path that bypasses
#   autosuggest, which the web runner has no command for today.
# ============================================================================

# ── Arrange ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
open ${base_site}
wait for result page load

# ── Act: search a term with no literal match ────────────────────────────────
search for ${junk_search_term}
wait 5 seconds
take screenshot as tc005_junk_results

# ── Assert: still on JustDial, on a real page ───────────────────────────────
store page url as junk_url
store page title as junk_title
verify stored junk_url contains "justdial"

# ── Assert: autosuggest resolved it rather than dead-ending ─────────────────
# The results heading must name whatever autosuggest matched. We deliberately do
# not assert the junk term itself appears — autosuggest replaces it, so the
# original string is gone from the visible page.
store text of heading_search_title as junk_resolved_heading

# ── Assert: the page is genuinely populated, not an empty shell ─────────────
store text of business_name as junk_first_business

# ── Assert: the page is still interactive — search box usable again ─────────
store attribute placeholder of search_box as junk_search_placeholder

take screenshot as tc005_verified
